---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { posts } from '../../data/resources.js';

const base = 'https://www.dg-sdk.com';
const canonical = base + '/blog';

---

<Layout
  title="Static Eliminator & Web Cleaning Technical Blog | Shidike"
  description="Practical guides on specifying, mounting and verifying anti static bars, ionizing air blowers and contact cleaning machines on real production lines."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: base },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: canonical }
    ]
  })} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Blog',
    name: 'Shidike Technical Blog',
    url: canonical,
    description: 'Guides on specifying, mounting and verifying anti static bars, ionizing air blowers and contact cleaning machines.',
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shidike', url: base },
    blogPost: posts.map(p => ({
      '@type': 'BlogPosting',
      headline: p.title,
      description: p.excerpt,
      url: canonical + '/' + p.slug,
      image: base + p.image + '.jpg',
      datePublished: '2026-09-01'
    }))
  })} />

  <section
    class="products-hero blog-hero-banner"
    style="background: #edf4fb url('/assets/img/static-eliminator/static-eliminator-category-banner.webp') center/86% auto no-repeat; background-attachment: scroll;"
  >
    <div class="container products-hero-inner">
      <span class="products-hero-kicker" data-aos="fade-down" data-aos-duration="600">Technical Blog</span>
      <h1 data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="700" data-aos-delay="100">Static Eliminators &amp; Web Cleaning, Explained</h1>
      <p data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="700" data-aos-delay="200">
        How to specify, mount and verify the equipment — written for the engineer who has to make it work on a line
        that is already running, not for a catalogue.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blog-list-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Blog</span></div>

      <div class="blog-intro">
        <p>
          Every article here starts in the same place: a line that is already built, already running, and
          that now has a static or contamination problem to solve without stopping production. So the
          guides deal in figures you can check against your own process &mdash; ion balance in volts, decay
          time in seconds, mounting distance in millimetres, air volume in CFM &mdash; rather than in feature
          lists.
        </p>
        <p>
          The static control articles cover how a pulsed AC and a pulsed DC bar behave at different
          distances from the web, why a bar that generates its high voltage internally from 24 V DC mounts
          differently from one fed by an external supply box, how to work out mounting pitch for a given
          bar length, and how to verify with a field meter or a charged plate monitor that the bar is
          still doing its job six months later. The industry pieces run the same problem for lithium
          battery electrode coating, slitting and winding, and for photovoltaic cell handling, backsheet
          lamination and glass loading, where the material and the line speed change the answer.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cleaning articles take the other half of the same problem. Charge attracts particles, and on
          optical film, polarizer, PCB and CCL surfaces it is the particle that causes the reject. Those
          guides work through tack values, belt against roller contact, single or double sided cleaning,
          and what a given cleanliness target asks of the machine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="blog-index-grid">
        {posts.map((post, i) => (
          <a href={`/blog/${post.slug}`} class="blog-index-card" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay={i * 100} data-aos-duration="600">
            <div class="blog-index-img">
              <picture>
                <source srcset={`${post.image}.webp`} type="image/webp" />
                <img src={`${post.image}.jpg`} alt={post.title} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              </picture>
            </div>
            <div class="blog-index-content">
              <div class="blog-index-tags">
                {post.tags.map(tag => <span class="blog-tag">{tag}</span>)}
              </div>
              <h2>{post.title}</h2>
              <p>{post.excerpt}</p>
              <div class="blog-index-meta">
                <span>{post.date}</span>
                <span>{post.readTime}</span>
              </div>
              <span class="blog-read-more">Read article &rarr;</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="blog-foot-note">
        These guides describe equipment Shidike builds:
        <a href="/products/static-eliminator">industrial static eliminators and ionizing bars</a> and
        <a href="/products/cleaning-machine">contact cleaning machines</a>. Background on how the
        technology works is in the <a href="/guides">static control guides</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* Use the same banner as every product and application page (.products-hero,
       520px) instead of .category-hero at 300px. */
    .blog-hero-banner h1 { color: #111; }
    .blog-list-section { padding: 44px 0 70px; background: #fff; }
    .blog-list-section .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 26px; font-size: 13.5px; color: #7d8d97; }
    .blog-list-section .breadcrumb a { color: var(--brand-deep); text-decoration: none; }
    .blog-list-section .breadcrumb span { margin: 0 8px; }

    .blog-intro {
      max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto 34px; color: var(--ink-muted, #55636d);
      font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.72;
    }
    .blog-intro p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .blog-intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .blog-index-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px;
      max-width: 1000px; margin-inline: auto;
    }
    .blog-index-card {
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden;
      text-decoration: none; color: inherit; transition: border-color .15s ease;
    }
    .blog-index-card:hover { border-color: var(--brand-deep); }
    .blog-index-img img {
      display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover;
    }
    .blog-index-content { padding: 18px 20px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1; }
    .blog-index-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .blog-tag {
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
      background: #eef4f8; color: #4a6373; padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 999px;
    }
    .blog-index-content h2 {
      font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.35; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 8px;
    }
    .blog-index-content p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .blog-index-meta {
      display: flex; gap: 14px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #8a99a4; margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .blog-read-more { margin-top: auto; font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brand-deep); }

    .blog-foot-note {
      max-width: 1000px; margin: 34px auto 0; padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
      font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-muted); text-align: center;
    }
    @media (max-width: 1000px) { .blog-index-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
    @media (max-width: 640px)  { .blog-index-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  </style>
</Layout>
